// FleetManagement/knip.jsonc
// Dead-code gate: unused files, exports and dependencies across all 13
// workspaces. Root cause this closes: nothing in the repo could see a dead
// export, so SUPPORTED_LOCALES in ops-web i18n.ts sat unused with ZERO
// consumers repo-wide while its sibling Locale union drifted into three
// hand-written copies. eslint no-unused-vars cannot see this: it works
// within a file, never across the import graph.
//
// ADOPTION STAGE 2 of 3 (knip.dev/guides/adopt-gradually). The documented
// burn-down order is files -> dependencies -> exports, because one unused
// FILE hides its own exports and deps, so files must reach zero first. It
// has: `knip --files` reports "Excellent, Knip found no issues", so that
// rule is PROMOTED TO ERROR here and a newly-orphaned file now fails the
// task instead of adding a gray line nobody reads.
//
// The remaining rules stay warn while their config is tuned. That is the
// same adoption reasoning //#typecheck:scripts documents: it stayed ungated
// at 89 errors precisely so the gate would not be born red, and was promoted
// only when the count reached zero by fixing every error at its root.
//
// NOT YET WIRED INTO __ci_fast__. That is stage 3, and it happens when the
// task as a whole can pass -- promoting one rule while others still warn
// makes the task's exit code meaningful for that rule alone, which is
// exactly the incremental ratchet the guide prescribes.
//
// Entry-point decisions, each from an observed hint rather than assumption:
//   apps/api            src/main.ts REMOVED -- redundant, the plugin
//                       already resolves the NestJS bootstrap.
//   packages/codemods   src/cli.ts REMOVED -- same, found via the bin/
//                       script parser.
//   driver/owner-app    index.js REMOVED -- no such file on develop. Both
//                       apps use main:expo-router/entry, so every file
//                       under app/ is a route entry reached only by the
//                       router and never imported. (dispatcher-app adds a
//                       custom index.js on the T17 branch; when that lands,
//                       its workspace entry must list index.js or the
//                       polyfill and the whole route tree read as dead.)
//   apps/ops-web        src/middleware.ts REMOVED -- no such file. App
//                       Router page/layout/route files are entry by
//                       convention. .css added to project so Tailwind
//                       imports are followed (hint: compiled extension
//                       excluded by project).
//
// ignoreBinaries lists SYSTEM binaries only -- tools installed on the HOST
// and resolvable from no package.json, so reporting them is a category
// error rather than a finding. adb (Android platform-tools), flock
// (util-linux) and railway (Railway CLI) were the original three; four more
// were added 2026-08-19 and every one is a host tool //#doctor already
// verifies as a machine CAPABILITY:
//   pre-commit  the hook framework bootstrap:machine installs
//   sops        SOPS, spawned by env-bootstrap-cli for decrypt/encrypt
//   age-keygen  the age identity tool machine-doctor probes for
//   eas         the Expo CLI the build-freshness gate queries
//   maestro     the mobile UI-test runner scripts/e2e/driver-maestro.mts
//               drives; surfaced only once the root project pattern was
//               widened to see .mts at all (2026-08-21)
// A machine missing any of them gets a named remediation from //#doctor,
// which is the right instrument for a host capability; knip reporting them
// as "unlisted" would be a second, weaker answer to a question already
// answered properly.
//
// ignoreDependencies, PER WORKSPACE, is the same classification fix one
// level down: a package that is DECLARED and USED, but consumed by SPAWNING
// A BINARY rather than by importing a module, is invisible to an
// import-graph analyser by construction.
//
// expo-doctor is exactly that, and this entry exists because PR #631
// created the false positive it answers. That PR moved the Expo dependency
// oracle off `npx expo-doctor@latest` -- a run-time registry fetch with no
// lockfile entry, no integrity hash and no review -- onto an EXACT
// devDependency of each Expo app, invoked through pnpm exec by
// scripts/expo-doctor-cli.ts. Pinning it was the security fix; the cost is
// that knip sees a declared package no file imports and calls it unused.
// Removing it to satisfy knip would restore the supply-chain hole, so the
// tool's model is what must be corrected, not the dependency.
//
// SCOPED TO THE TWO EXPO WORKSPACES rather than declared globally: a
// root-level ignore would also exempt any future workspace that declares
// expo-doctor and genuinely does not use it, which is precisely the finding
// this gate should still make.
//
// @sentry/cli is the SAME CLASS and was ALMOST REMOVED IN ERROR (2026-08-22).
// The reasoning that nearly deleted it: `pnpm why` shows @sentry/cli reached
// TWICE -- directly as a devDependency AND transitively through
// @sentry/react-native@7.11.0, which depends on the very same 2.58.4. It reads
// like the redundant root-workspace declaration knip documents, so both apps
// had it removed.
//
// RUNTIME REFUTED THAT. After removal, `pnpm exec sentry-cli` from
// apps/owner-app answered "Command not found". pnpm's strict isolation exposes
// binaries from DIRECT dependencies only; a transitive package is resolvable
// as a MODULE while its bin is absent from the workspace PATH. `pnpm why`
// answers a package-graph question, not a bin-resolution one -- a different
// oracle, exactly like knip's import graph versus a spawned binary.
//
// WHY IT MATTERS THAT THIS FAILS QUIETLY: app.json configures the
// @sentry/react-native/expo plugin, which uploads bundles and source maps
// during EAS builds by SHELLING OUT to sentry-cli. A missing bin would not
// fail `pnpm install`; it would fail on an EAS builder, and the symptom is
// unsymbolicated production stack traces -- a defect visible only after a
// crash report arrives useless.
//
// drizzle-kit: THIS COMMENT WAS WRONG until 2026-08-19 and is corrected here.
// It claimed scripts/db-generate.ts invokes drizzle-kit from the ROOT while it
// is declared in apps/driver-app -- "a genuine misplacement". Ground truth
// says otherwise: apps/api runs "tsx ../../scripts/db-generate.ts", so the cwd
// is apps/api, where drizzle-kit IS correctly declared. The root workspace
// never resolves it, so knip's unlisted-binary line is an artefact of
// attributing scripts/ to the root by path.
//
// The driver-app declaration is real and is NOT a misplacement either: Expo
// requires drizzle-kit to GENERATE the migrations an app bundles, because each
// phone holds an isolated database and there is no server-side migrate step.
// That pipeline does not exist yet in driver-app (no drizzle.config.ts, no
// drizzle/ folder, no .sql files, no migrate() call, no .sql in Metro
// sourceExts, no babel.config.js), so the dependency is the idle half of work
// never started -- tracked as its own device-verified arc, with
// storage-schema-drift.guard.test.ts holding the line meanwhile.
//
// It stays UNIGNORED on purpose: an ignore entry would silence the one signal
// pointing at that gap.
//
// THE ROOT ignoreDependencies IS A PLUGIN GAP, and it is the ONLY entry here
// added as a last resort rather than a classification fix. knip's Semantic
// Release plugin IS enabled and DOES resolve .releaserc.json -- `knip --debug`
// shows it emit exactly one dependency from that file,
// "deferResolve:@semantic-release/changelog". But the same plugins array also
// names @semantic-release/github (as a plugin) and conventionalcommits (as the
// preset for commit-analyzer and release-notes-generator), and the plugin's
// dependency finder reports neither. That is knip's documented false-positive
// shape: "if a plugin exists and the dependency is referenced in the
// configuration file, but its custom dependency finder does not detect it,
// then that is a false positive" -- and its guidance is to fix the plugin
// upstream, with ignoreDependencies as the last resort. Both packages are
// load-bearing: dropping either breaks `pnpm release` on main.
//
// SCOPED TO THE ROOT workspace, not declared globally, so a future workspace
// that declares them and genuinely does not use them is still reported.
{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",
  "ignoreBinaries": [
    "adb",
    "age-keygen",
    "eas",
    "flock",
    "maestro",
    "pre-commit",
    "railway",
    "sops"
  ],
  "rules": {
    "files": "error",
    "dependencies": "warn",
    "devDependencies": "warn",
    "unlisted": "warn",
    "unresolved": "warn",
    "binaries": "warn",
    "exports": "warn",
    "types": "warn",
    "nsExports": "warn",
    "nsTypes": "warn",
    "enumMembers": "warn",
    "duplicates": "warn"
  },
  "workspaces": {
    ".": {
      "ignoreDependencies": [
        "@semantic-release/github",
        "conventional-changelog-conventionalcommits"
      ],
      "entry": [
        "scripts/**/*.{ts,mts}"
      ],
      "project": [
        "scripts/**/*.{ts,mts}",
        "*.{mjs,cjs,js}"
      ],
      "includeEntryExports": true
    },
    "apps/api": {
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.ts"
      ]
    },
    "apps/ops-web": {
      "entry": [
        "src/app/**/{page,layout,route,template,error,loading,not-found}.tsx",
        "src/app/**/{page,layout,route,template,error,loading,not-found}.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}"
      ]
    },
    "apps/driver-app": {
      "entry": [
        "app/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
        "app/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
      ],
      "ignoreDependencies": [
        "expo-doctor",
        "@sentry/cli"
      ]
    },
    "apps/owner-app": {
      "entry": [
        "app/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
        "app/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
      ],
      "ignoreDependencies": [
        "expo-doctor",
        "@sentry/cli"
      ]
    },
    "workers/main-worker": {
      "entry": [
        "src/index.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.ts"
      ]
    },
    "packages/domain": {
      "entry": [
        "src/index.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.ts"
      ]
    },
    "packages/sync-protocol": {
      "entry": [
        "src/index.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.ts"
      ]
    },
    "packages/observability": {
      "entry": [
        "src/index.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.ts"
      ]
    },
    "packages/design-tokens": {
      "entry": [
        "src/index.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.ts"
      ]
    },
    "packages/codemods": {
      "entry": [
        "src/index.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.ts"
      ]
    },
    "packages/test-fixtures": {
      "entry": [
        "src/index.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.ts"
      ]
    },
    "e2e": {
      "entry": [
        "**/*.spec.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "**/*.ts"
      ]
    }
  }
}
